< Important points to follow while make dockerfiles >

1. Use supported base images

2. Prefer Alpine/slim/distroless where appropriate: To reduce image size by ignoring unwanted data or cache data. If the image size is large, container lifetime will decrease and crashes very soon

3. Use multi-stage builds

4. Don't run as root: to restrict access to root if there are any malicious attacks

| RUN chown -R nginx:nginx /usr/share/nginx/html/ | nginx is present by default |

| RUN chown -R nginx:nginx /usr/share/nginx/html/  USER nginx | change the login to nginx |

5. No secrets in dockerfile
6. Use .dockerignore
7. Pin application dependencies
8. No unnecessary packages
9. Do not use latest versions in production: because latest tag will be assigned to the newer versions.
10. Scan image with Trivy

# To scan image with trivy. Install trivy.

| trivy image image-name |

FROM nginx:alpine
RUN rm -rf /usr/share/nginx/html/*
EXPOSE 80
MAINTAINER pavan
COPY index.html /usr/share/nginx/html/
RUN chown -R nginx:nginx /usr/share/nginx/html/
CMD ["nginx", "-g", "daemon off;"]

FROM httpd:2.4-alpine
RUN rm -rf /usr/local/alpine2/htdocs/*
COPY index.html /usr/local/alpine2/htdocs
EXPOSE 80
RUN adduser -D new-user
RUN chown -R new-user:new-user /usr/local/alpine2/htdocs
USER new-user
CMD ["httpd-foreground"]

FROM node:22-alpine
WORKDIR /myapp
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm install --production
COPY --chown=node:node . .
USER node
EXPOSE 80
CMD ["node", "index.js"]














